  "tagline": "In-memory, typo-tolerant search engine in C++ with vector, hybrid and conversational search.",
  "description": "Typesense is an open-source search engine that keeps its index in RAM for consistently low-latency, typo-tolerant queries and pitches itself as a self-hostable Algolia alternative. Beyond keyword search it supports vector and hybrid search with built-in embedding models, joins between collections, geo search and a conversational (RAG) endpoint. Clustering uses Raft for high availability, but every node holds the full dataset, so capacity is bounded by the RAM of one machine. It is GPL-3.0 licensed, with Typesense Cloud as the managed option.",
